 ## Failure modes
 
-1. **Identity-record rename desync.** If the writer (`session-setup.sh`) and reader (`lib-resolve-implement-tmpdir.sh`) are not changed together, `/implement` Stop/SessionStart hooks stop binding and lose halt protection. Earliest signal: resolver / sessionstart-health harness failures. Mitigation: change writer + reader + all sentinel-writing test fixtures in the same PR; run the resolver harness.
+1. **Identity-record rename desync.** If the writer (`session-setup.sh`) and reader (`lib-resolve-implement-tmpdir.sh`) are not changed together, `/implement` Stop/SessionStart hooks stop binding and lose halt protection. Earliest signal: resolver / sessionstart-health harness failures. Mitigation: change writer + reader + all sentinel-writing test fixtures in the same PR; run the resolver harness; keep a read-only `.larch-keepalive` fallback for pre-rollout in-flight sessions.
 2. **Self-deletion of the running version.** If `/upgrade-larch` runs from a version outside the 8-newest-installed, that dir is pruned; concurrent jobs on it lose their dir. Signal: a "version blown away" report for a very old running version. Mitigation: just-installed always kept; running version kept iff in the newest-8 (matches the user's "<8 releases" expectation); `rm` of an open inode does not kill the running process, and the user restarts post-upgrade. Documented tradeoff, accepted in Round 1.
 3. **Legacy-dir mtime mis-ordering during migration.** Pre-feature dirs whose mtime was bumped by the now-removed touch may briefly sort newer than their true install order. Signal: a touched old version outranking a fresh install in the keep-8 set. Mitigation: every `/upgrade-larch` install writes a stamp, so the newest entries become stamp-ordered immediately; mtime fallback only affects un-stamped legacy dirs, which age out. Low impact.
+4. **Retained-set off-by-one.** Seeding `$ACTUAL_VERSION` after selecting the first 8 can leave 9 dirs. Mitigation: seed first, then fill to `KEEP_VERSIONS`, and assert exactly 8 remain in the target-outside-top-8/stamp-failure test.
 
